Defines the different journals (Sales, Purchase, Cash, Bank, General, etc.) that control how journal entries are created, posted, and numbered in the accounting system.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Sales journal, Purchase journal, Cash journal, Bank journal
Bank & Cash management (reconciliation source)
Miscellaneous / General journal for manual adjustments
Control default accounts, sequences, and posting restrictions
Multi-company, multi-currency, and type-specific behavior
Used in invoices, payments, bank statements, and asset depreciation

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), code (char, required, unique per company)
type (selection: sale, purchase, cash, bank, general, opening, closing…)
default_account_id, payment_credit_account_id, payment_debit_account_id
sequence_id → ir.sequence (for entry numbering)
company_id, currency_id
bank_account_id (for bank journals)
post_at (bank statements), refund_sequence

Critical Hooks: action_create_bank_statements, _get_journal_dashboard, onchange_type
Security: account.group_account_manager + journal-specific record rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
journal, accounting journal, sales journal, purchase journal, bank journal, cash journal, general journal, journal code, journal type, journal entry source, posting journal, misc journal, journal sequence
Related Models (most joined):

account.account (default accounts)
account.move (via journal_id)
account.bank.statement
account.payment
ir.sequence
res.bank / res.partner.bank

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
account.journal is the core Odoo model defining accounting journals with type (sale/purchase/bank/cash/general), code, default accounts, sequence, and company settings. It controls journal entry creation, automatic numbering, default accounts on invoices/payments, bank reconciliation, and posting behavior across the entire accounting module. Heavily referenced by account.move, account.payment, account.bank.statement, and all financial workflows.